-- title:
--   Degree one places: residue field generated by constants
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$ in the sense of the project's structure `Place`: a valuation subring of $F$ whose underlying set contains the image of every element of $K$ under the structure map $K \to F$, which is not the whole of $F$, and which is a principal ideal ring. Its residue field `v.ResidueField` is the residue field of this valuation subring viewed as a local ring, and its degree `v.deg` is defined as $\operatorname{finrank}_K$ of that residue field, i.e. the dimension of the residue field as a $K$-vector space, with the usual Mathlib convention that the value is $0$ when no finite basis exists. The theorem asserts the equivalence: $v.\mathrm{deg} = 1$ if and only if the structure map $K \to v.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective as a function. No further hypotheses are imposed; in particular nothing is assumed about $F/K$ being finitely generated or separable, and nothing is asserted about the existence of such places.
--
--   This is the standard dictionary between the two phrasings of a rational place of a function field: a place of degree one, and a place whose residue field is exhausted by the constants. It is used throughout the project to pass between these forms, for instance in the descent statements for divisors under a constant field extension and in the construction of places with prescribed restriction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_deg_eq_one_iff_surjective_algebraMap_residueField.lean

import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
